"task","acceptance","controller_implementation","other_numerical_settings"],"fixed_controller":"controller.gvs_nmpc@7.0.0","hypothesis":"Over the granted box holding_tip_speed_weight in [0.05, 1.0] and terminal_tip_speed_weight in [0.0, 1.0], no bounded coordinate change of these two tip-speed weights can bring the sampled final-window holding speed near the 0.02 m/s limit or attain joint reach+holding acceptance: the two tip-speed weights are a low-yield lever, and the residual sampled holding violation is dominated by mechanisms outside the allowed variable set (solver/compute budget saturation and task-end horizon clipping). This batch is a bounded falsification test of that claim, not a promotion of any candidate.","max_candidates":6,"method":"search.family_coordinate@1.0.0","objectives":["joint_reach_holding_acceptance","terminal_error_m","holding_max_error_m","holding_max_speed_m_s","complete_update_s"],"planned_budget":{"backend_solves":6,"model_calls":6,"tool_calls":24,"wall_s":5940.0,"worker_calls":0},"rationale":"Authored from the accepted revision (73f4c6aca1442274b428e42beca4fc1de800d0f5766924042680130eb70a1dae) and the performed saved-state/plans-view check (proposal c7009cb627549f7727a56ee829acbbc3a71e88f179f1afba66c349551ae05cf6, result a7470ffa6dc4cb722ff1dff64220334838f6545199014923029eee2bc9dd1fb6), together with the sealed comparison (F141 = physical_tradeoff). The permitted variables are exactly the two tip-speed recipe weights, and the evidence shows the single tested change (holding 0.0 -> 0.05 with terminal 0.0 fixed, F284/F433/F467) moved sampled hold speed by only F388 = -0.4060100069642385 m/s from F297 to F289, leaving it roughly 59x F452 while joint acceptance stayed false (F9) and mean complete-update time rose (F273 vs F11/F346). Because the observed reduction is a small fraction of the gap and the weight ceiling is 1.0 (only ~20x the tested 0.05), the honest promise that this bounded coordinate batch attains joint acceptance is 'unlikely'; its scientific value is bounding/falsifying the weight lever and documenting the response surface as a partial monotonicity check. The method supplies candidate ask/tell only, so every candidate still requires candidate.apply, simulation.run, evaluation.run and control.profile_report, followed by frozen bound_comparison and diagnostic_revision; the plan executes nothing, promotes no candidate, and needs a future grant. Local/raw weighted objectives are not ranked across weights (F313) and computation is reported separately (F419), so acceptance is judged jointly first and then componentwise on terminal_error_m, holding_max_error_m and holding_max_speed_m_s. Planned budget follows the required form: backend_solves = max_candidates = 6, tool_calls = 24 >= 4*6, wall_s = 5940 >= 990*6, worker_calls = 0, with provider/backend attempts to be stated if retries are required. The dominant candidate mechanisms (budget-truncated plan selection and task-end horizon clipping) lie outside the granted variable set and are recorded as fidelity limits rather than varied here; the plan therefore does not select improvement-96f0ade35119 and keeps recommendation acceptance separate from candidate selection. A coordinate step of 0.2 keeps all generated points at 0.0 or at least 0.05, avoiding any forbidden tiny positive values inside (0, 0.0001). Fixed conditions are recorded here in full because the plan validator accepts only the bare category tokens in fixed_conditions: robot = the sealed multi-segment tendon-driven soft-robot definition (robot.xml) with six tendon routes and per-tendon 8.0 N force limit F247, as used by execution 087adee8e8a24fe88e5c85fe89e638c8; task = family task.reach (task_id family-multisegment-dev, identity 24eb233a2e36d7194994c416207bf05f3ff644db2ed02c8a50496f8c3dc4b041) with target_position_m [0.29, 0.035, 0.19] (F212), simulated duration 0.35 s and control/sample period 0.01 s (F128, F417, F521); acceptance = platform.acceptance_definition@1.0.0 with terminal tolerance 0.01 m (F252), final holding window 0.05 s (F524), holding position limit 0.01 m (F441) and holding speed limit 0.02 m/s (F452), joint reach+holding acceptance required and comparison rule F241 at tolerance F43 = 1e-09; controller_implementation = controller.gvs_nmpc@7.0.0 frozen (F516, F522) with only control/recipe/holding_tip_speed_weight (F194) and control/recipe/terminal_tip_speed_weight (F467) allowed to vary, no code, horizon or solver-setting change; other_numerical_settings = evaluator evaluate.reach@1.0.0 with tolerance_m 0.01 (F252), execution model model.serial_bending_cells@1.0.0, saved-state model model.gvs@1.0.0 at a 0.01 s horizon with implicit_euler 0.002 s, recipe horizon 10 and max_iterations 120 (F520) and max_cpu_s 30.0 (F517), all other recipe, timing and evaluator values held at the accepted baseline. The newly read plans-view result (a7470ffa6dc4cb722ff1dff64220334838f6545199014923029eee2bc9dd1fb6) is cited as per-update aliases F640, F664, F657, F695, F667, F676, F671, F702, F724, F658, F673, and the required candidate-profile result aliases F454, F458, F469, F471 are included for any new measured fact.","scientific_promise":"unlikely","step":0.2,"stopping_conditions":["Stop after max_candidates coordinate candidates are evaluated, or earlier when the planned backend_solves, tool_calls or wall_s budget is exhausted.","Halt the batch immediately and report if any candidate returns valid_complete_execution false, solver_error_count > 0, or a per-tendon force-bound violation.","Conclude that the weight-only lever remains low-yield if no candidate attains joint_reach_holding_passed true and no candidate reduces holding_max_speed_m_s beyond the already-observed 0.4060100069642385 m/s reduction toward the 0.02 m/s limit.","Conclude the low-yield claim is falsified if some candidate attains joint_reach_holding_passed true (reach passes and both holding limits pass), or shows a strongly interactive weight effect as described in the weakening observations.","Do not exceed the declared budget, and do not select or promote any candidate in this stage: no execution is authorized and any validated plan requires a future grant."],"variables":{"control/recipe/holding_tip_speed_weight":[0.05,1.0],"control/recipe/terminal_tip_speed_weight":[0.0,1.0]},"verification":["candidate.apply","simulation.run","evaluation.run","control.profile_report","bound_comparison","diagnostic_revision"],"version":"1.0.0","weakening_observations":["Any bounded candidate inside the searched box that attains holding_max_speed_m_s <= 0.02 m/s together with holding_max_error_m <= 0.01 m and terminal_error_m <= 0.01 m (joint_reach_holding_passed true) would falsify the low-yield claim.","A monotone, roughly proportional fall of holding_max_speed_m_s toward the 0.02 m/s limit as the weights rise (rather than saturation or worsening) would weaken the claim that the lever is uniformly low-yield.","A large additional hold-speed reduction obtained only when both weights are raised together (strong interaction) would weaken the claim that the lever is low-yield, since the single tested point held terminal_tip_speed_weight at 0.0.","Candidate-to-candidate variation in holding_max_speed_m_s that does not order with the weights at all would weaken the claim that weight changes act in the intended direction, and would instead point to run-to-run or solver-driven variation."]},"required_fresh_steps":["bound_comparison","candidate.apply","control.profile_report","diagnostic_revision","evaluation.run","simulation.run"],"requires_future_grant":true,"scientific_promise":"unlikely","screening":{"local_screening":"none","raw_weighted_objectives_are_physical_ranking":false},"semantic_status":"Model-authored promise and causal reasoning are separate from operational validation.","structurally_operationally_valid":true}